window.MK_SEARCH=[{"p":"Home","s":"","u":"","x":"Documentation for Mood Kit, the one-click horror mood pack for Unreal Engine 5.2 and newer: moods, weather, lamps, Mood Events and Blueprint nodes.","k":"page","i":"sparkle"},{"p":"Getting started","s":"","u":"getting-started/","x":"Add the pack, open the Mood Gallery and see your level change in one click.","k":"page","i":"rocket"},{"p":"Getting started","s":"Start in one minute","u":"getting-started/#start-in-one-minute","x":"Add the pack to your project. Everything is in Content > MoodKit . Open your level. Any level works, even an empty one. Open the panel once. In the Content Drawer, open MoodKit , right-click EUW_MoodGallery and choose Run Editor Utility Widget . You only do th","k":"section"},{"p":"Getting started","s":"Open it again later","u":"getting-started/#open-it-again","x":"After the first time, open the panel with the Mood Kit button in the toolbar (it has a small fog icon), or from Tools > Mood Gallery . If you leave the panel docked, it comes back with the editor, and so does the button. Why the first open is a right-click A p","k":"section"},{"p":"Getting started","s":"The normal order","u":"getting-started/#order","x":"Every time you use Mood Kit, you go in the same order. 01 Preview Click a card. Your level is not changed, and nothing is saved. 02 Apply to Level Adds BP_MoodDirector with the mood, sliders, parts and weather you chose. 03 Play The mood starts with the game. ","k":"section"},{"p":"Getting started","s":"What is in the pack","u":"getting-started/#in-the-pack","x":"In Content > MoodKit What it is EUW_MoodGallery The Mood Gallery panel. Right-click it and choose Run Editor Utility Widget, once. Levels > Lvl_MoodLab A test level with a corridor, rooms, a basement and a courtyard. Moods The 22 moods, named DA_... . Pick one","k":"section"},{"p":"Getting started","s":"Next","u":"getting-started/#next","x":"The Mood Gallery The panel at the side of the editor. Three tabs, Moods, Fit and Place, and nothing changes until you click Apply. The moods Every horror mood, seen in the Mood Lab corridor and on an open level, with the weather each one brings. Fit to your le","k":"section"},{"p":"The Mood Gallery","s":"","u":"mood-gallery/","x":"The panel at the side of the editor. Three tabs, Moods, Fit and Place, and nothing changes until you click Apply.","k":"page","i":"panel"},{"p":"The Mood Gallery","s":"The Moods tab","u":"mood-gallery/#moods-tab","x":"Click a card to see the mood on your level. Moving from one mood to the next blends smoothly in under a second. Point at the numbered dots to see what each part does. 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 1 Three tabs Moods to pick a look, Fit to suit your level, Place to add lamps, ","k":"section"},{"p":"The Mood Gallery","s":"The Fit tab","u":"mood-gallery/#fit-tab","x":"Every level is different, so every mood can be shifted to suit yours. All of it is explained in Fit a mood to your level . 1 2 3 4 5 1 Fit to this level Brightness and Level lamps in stops, Fog and Surface wear in percent. Reset puts them back. 2 Weather Mood'","k":"section"},{"p":"The Mood Gallery","s":"The Place tab","u":"mood-gallery/#place-tab","x":"Everything you add to the level: lamps, rooms and events, and what your own lights do. 1 2 3 4 5 1 Mood lamps Click a style and a lamp appears where you look, fixed to the ceiling, wall or floor. 2 How many and Spacing For Fill a Row and Fill a Grid. 3 Fill a ","k":"section"},{"p":"The Mood Gallery","s":"Always at the bottom","u":"mood-gallery/#bottom","x":"The bottom of the panel stays the same on every tab. Part What it does Name and summary Of the mood on screen now. Test Blackout Cuts the lights for about 3 seconds, then brings them back. Grey while no mood is on. Back to Original Your level as you built it. ","k":"section"},{"p":"The Mood Gallery","s":"Previews are safe","u":"mood-gallery/#safe","x":"A preview never changes your level. Your lights are put back before every save, copy and Play, and the preview actor is never saved. Closing the panel ends the preview. Opening another level starts again from Original. A light you add during a preview joins th","k":"section"},{"p":"The 22 moods","s":"","u":"moods/","x":"Every horror mood, seen in the Mood Lab corridor and on an open level, with the weather each one brings.","k":"page","i":"moon"},{"p":"The 22 moods","s":"Every mood","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Click a card to see it large. Switch between the Mood Lab corridor and an open level, and hold the button to see the same view with no mood. The arrow keys move between moods. All 22 Indoors Outdoors Clear Sealed Dark No light but what you carry. Heavy, wet ai","k":"section"},{"p":"The 22 moods","s":"Lighting looks","u":"moods/#lighting-looks","x":"Eight moods are each built around one classic lighting setup, the way a film lights a scene: Blinds Drawn. Hard light through half-shut blinds, in bars across floors and walls. Best where the sun falls on a floor. Sodium Night. Orange street lamps over wet gro","k":"section"},{"p":"The 22 moods","s":"Works on your level","u":"moods/#your-level","x":"Moods are made for any level: a finished environment, a blockout, or an empty level with nothing but a floor. Drag across each picture to compare. Original Moonlit Exposure The open Third Person level. The mood brings its own moon, clouds, fog and wet ground. ","k":"section"},{"p":"The 22 moods","s":"What a mood is made of","u":"moods/#made-of","x":"Sky. A moon or sun, stars and moving clouds, all from one material that lights your level. Some moods bring a black sun, a huge red moon or a sky that glows after sunset. Light. The sun or moon, the soft light from the sky, your level's lamps, pools of light t","k":"section"},{"p":"The 22 moods","s":"The first click","u":"moods/#first-click","x":"The first mood you click after opening the project can take up to a minute to look right, because Unreal prepares its materials. You may see a grey or plain picture during that time. It only happens once.","k":"section"},{"p":"The 22 moods","s":"All moods at a glance","u":"moods/#at-a-glance","x":"Mood Weather Summary Sealed Dark DA_SealedDark Clear No light but what you carry. Heavy, wet air. Failing Power DA_FailingPower Clear Weak, sick lamps stutter and die one by one. Blind Fog DA_BlindFog Light Ash Pale fog swallows the world, and ash drifts down ","k":"section"},{"p":"The 22 moods","s":"Use a mood in your game","u":"moods/#use","x":"In the editor: click a card, then Apply to Level . See Apply and play . From a Blueprint: the Set Mood node, with Blend Seconds to fade. See Blueprint nodes . When the player walks somewhere: a Mood Zone or a Mood Event. See Mood Events and zones .","k":"section"},{"p":"Fit a mood to your level","s":"","u":"fit/","x":"The Brightness, Level lamps, Fog and Surface wear sliders, the sun and moon, and the 13 parts you can switch off.","k":"page","i":"sliders"},{"p":"Fit a mood to your level","s":"Fit to this level","u":"fit/#sliders","x":"Four sliders shift the mood without changing it. Try three of them below, on real pictures from the Mood Lab taken at three values each. Brightness Fog Surface wear Brightness 0.0 Slider Range Starts at What it does Brightness -3 to +3 stops 0 Shifts the whole","k":"section"},{"p":"Fit a mood to your level","s":"Weather","u":"fit/#weather","x":"The Weather list and its sliders sit under the four sliders. They are explained in Weather .","k":"section"},{"p":"Fit a mood to your level","s":"Sun and moon","u":"fit/#sun-and-moon","x":"Each mood picks where its light comes from. To keep one direction in every mood, aim it yourself. Slider Range Starts at What it does Turn 0° to 360° 0° The direction the light comes from, around the level. Moving it ticks Aim it myself. Height 0° to 90° 30° T","k":"section"},{"p":"Fit a mood to your level","s":"Parts","u":"fit/#parts","x":"Each mood is made of parts. Untick any part your level already does well, and your level keeps its own version of it. Point at a part in the panel to read what it does. Sky The mood's sky with its moon, stars and clouds. Off keeps your own sky. Sun and moon li","k":"section"},{"p":"Fit a mood to your level","s":"Keep it","u":"fit/#keep","x":"Apply to Level saves the sliders, weather, parts, sun aim and wind with the level, on the BP_MoodDirector actor. To keep what you set as a mood of your own, for any level, use Save as My Mood .","k":"section"},{"p":"Make your own mood","s":"","u":"your-own-moods/","x":"Save as My Mood keeps what you set on the Fit tab. Customize This Mood opens every value. An update never touches your moods.","k":"page","i":"palette"},{"p":"Make your own mood","s":"Save as My Mood","u":"your-own-moods/#save-as-my-mood","x":"The quick way. Set the mood up on the Fit tab, then click Save as My Mood at the bottom of it. FIT TAB Brightness +1 Fog 50% Rain 150% ☐ Surface wear My Drowned MoodKit / MyMoods SLIDERS GO BACK Brightness 0 Fog 100% Rain 100% The picture stays the same What o","k":"section"},{"p":"Make your own mood","s":"Customize This Mood","u":"your-own-moods/#customize","x":"For every value. Pick the mood closest to what you want, then click Customize This Mood on the Place tab. A copy is made in MoodKit > MyMoods , with its own card at the end, named like Failing Power Custom . A window opens with every value of the mood, in 12 g","k":"section"},{"p":"Make your own mood","s":"Colours mean what they look like","u":"your-own-moods/#colours","x":"Colours and levels in a mood mean what they look like on screen, because the mood sets the exposure itself. A value of 0.18 reads as middle grey on any level, however it was lit.","k":"section"},{"p":"Make your own mood","s":"Delete a mood of your own","u":"your-own-moods/#delete","x":"Close the panel first. Then, in MoodKit > MyMoods , right-click the mood, for example DA_Drowned_Mine , and choose Delete . Your own weathers and lamp styles The same idea works for weathers and lamp styles . They live in MyWeather and MyLampStyles .","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather","s":"","u":"weather/","x":"Nine weathers on top of any mood. Floors soak and dry, snow and ash settle and melt, and one wind moves everything.","k":"page","i":"rain"},{"p":"Weather","s":"The 9 weathers","u":"weather/#weathers","x":"Every picture is the same courtyard in the same mood, Moonlit Exposure, with the ground as it looks once the weather has been going for a while. Clear Drizzle Rain Storm Dry Lightning Snow Blizzard Ash Light Ash Rain Snow or ash Wet ground Settles Lightning Wi","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather","s":"Put a weather on a mood","u":"weather/#put-a-weather-on-a-mood","x":"Every mood comes with a weather of its own: Drowned brings Rain, Blind Fog brings Light Ash and Ash Fall brings Ash. The others bring Clear. You can put any weather on any mood. In the editor: on the Fit tab, pick from the Weather list. Mood's own keeps the on","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather","s":"The ground builds up","u":"weather/#ground","x":"Rain soaks the floors and fills puddles over time, and they dry slowly after it stops. Snow and ash settle on everything that faces up, and melt away when the weather changes. RAIN FALLS CLEAR AGAIN wet dry time the mood's own damp Soak Seconds Dry Seconds 10x","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather","s":"One wind for everything","u":"weather/#wind","x":"Direction 19.3° by default N Rain slants Snow drifts Clouds and fog roll Hanging lamps sway Branch shadows move Gusts come and go Rain slants, snow drifts, clouds and fog roll, and branch shadows and hanging lamps sway, all with the same wind, its gusts and it","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather","s":"Turn it up or down","u":"weather/#turn-it-up-or-down","x":"Slider Range Starts at What it does Rain 0% to 200% 100% The weather's rain. Also turns down the lens drops and puddle rings. Snow and ash 0% to 200% 100% The weather's falling snow or ash. Dust and embers 0% to 200% 100% The mood's own dust and embers. Lightn","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather","s":"Make your own weather","u":"weather/#make-your-own-weather","x":"A weather is an asset, so a new one needs no code. Duplicate a weather from MoodKit > Core > Weather , such as WX_Snow . Move the copy into a folder named MyWeather inside MoodKit. Open it and change it. Its groups are Card, Rain, Snow and Ash, Ground, Build U","k":"section"},{"p":"Storms and lightning","s":"","u":"storms/","x":"How a lightning strike works, striking when you want, keeping flashing light safe, and Weather Zones.","k":"page","i":"bolt"},{"p":"Storms and lightning","s":"How a strike works","u":"storms/#strike","x":"0 s 2 s 4 s 6 s 8 s 10 s 12 s Strike: up to 3 flashes, 0.4 s apart Strike Strike at least 4 s between strikes Never more than 3 flashes a second. A strike flashes one to three times , 0.4 seconds apart, so never more than 3 times a second. Strikes come at leas","k":"section"},{"p":"Storms and lightning","s":"Strike when you want","u":"storms/#test-lightning","x":"Test Lightning on the Fit tab strikes at once, in any weather. Trigger Lightning does the same from a Blueprint. Good for a scare. A Mood Event with Lightning ticked strikes as the player walks in. The Lightning slider sets how often a weather strikes by itsel","k":"section"},{"p":"Storms and lightning","s":"Flashing light and your players","u":"storms/#safety","x":"Warn your players Strikes and flickering lamps stay under the common limit for flashing light: at most 3 flashes a second, and strikes at least 4 seconds apart. Some players are still affected by flashing light. Warn them if your game has it, and let them turn","k":"section"},{"p":"Storms and lightning","s":"Weather Zones","u":"storms/#weather-zones","x":"A Weather Zone changes the weather while the player is inside it: a storm on the cliffs, snow in the mountains. Add one with Add Weather Zone on the Place tab, or drag BP_MoodWeatherZone from MoodKit > Core , then scale it.","k":"section"},{"p":"Storms and lightning","s":"Weather Zone (BP_MoodWeatherZone)","u":"storms/#wzone-weather-zone-bp-moodweatherzone","x":"Value Range Default What it does Weather weather asset empty The weather while the player is inside, such as WX_Snow or WX_Storm. Leave empty for the mood's own weather. Blend Seconds number 0 to 30 5 How long the change of weather takes. Restore On Exit switc","k":"section"},{"p":"Indoor rooms","s":"","u":"indoor-rooms/","x":"Interior volumes tell Mood Kit where your roofs are. Rain and fog banks stay outside, and rooms get their own brightness and fog.","k":"page","i":"house"},{"p":"Indoor rooms","s":"Add an interior volume","u":"indoor-rooms/#add","x":"Look at the room in the 3D view. Click Add Interior Volume on the Place tab. A blue box appears where you look, already selected. Scale it to fit the room: press R in the 3D view and drag a handle. Ctrl + Z removes it again. You can also drag BP_MoodInterior f","k":"section"},{"p":"Indoor rooms","s":"What stays outside","u":"indoor-rooms/#outside","x":"Inside a volume there is no rain, no rain marks or puddle rings, no drops on the lens, and no falling or settled snow. The wind does not reach hanging lamps, and the fog bank stays out. Dust in the air stays, and ash lets a little drift in.","k":"section"},{"p":"Indoor rooms","s":"A room's own light and fog","u":"indoor-rooms/#own-light","x":"While the view is inside, a room can have its own brightness and fog, the way eyes adjust to a dark room. Select the volume and set its values under Interior .","k":"section"},{"p":"Indoor rooms","s":"Interior volume (BP_MoodInterior)","u":"indoor-rooms/#room-interior-volume-bp-moodinterior","x":"Value Range Default What it does Brightness number -3 to 3 0 Shifts the exposure while the view is inside, in stops. Positive is brighter, as eyes adjust to a dark room. Fog Amount number 0 to 2 1 Multiplies the height fog while the view is inside. 1 is as the","k":"section"},{"p":"Indoor rooms","s":"Good to know","u":"indoor-rooms/#good-to-know","x":"Rain, snow and fog banks stop at the first 8 rooms . More rooms still change brightness and fog. Lightning lights a room only through its doors and windows. On your own levels, rain comes indoors until you add volumes. The Mood Lab has three: the corridor, the","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Lamps","s":"","u":"lamps/","x":"Lamps you place, move and copy like any actor. The mood sets how bright each one is and its colour.","k":"page","i":"lamp"},{"p":"Mood Lamps","s":"Place a lamp","u":"lamps/#place","x":"Look where you want the lamp in the 3D view. Click its style on the Place tab: Hanging, Bulb, Wall, Street, Candle, Work light, Beacon or Light only. The lamp appears where you look, fixed to the ceiling, wall or floor, and it is selected. Move it with the arr","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Lamps","s":"Lamp settings","u":"lamps/#settings","x":"Select a lamp and find these in the Details panel, under Mood Lamp . Setting What it does Style How the lamp looks and shines. Pick any Lamp Style asset. Brightness , Colour , Reach Multiply the style's brightness, colour and how far the light reaches. Cone De","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Lamps","s":"Many at once","u":"lamps/#many","x":"Fill a Row How many 6, Spacing 4 m 4 m Fill a Grid shared over a selected room Fill a Row and Fill a Grid add as many lamps as How many says, Spacing apart, around where you look, in the style of the selected lamp or the last style you used. With an interior v","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Lamps","s":"Swinging lamps","u":"lamps/#sway","x":"Set Sway Degrees and a hanging lamp swings like a pendulum, with its light and shadows. Only lamps that hang can swing. Outdoors it swings along the wind , harder in a strong wind. Inside an interior volume it keeps its own swing. It swings in the game, and in","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Lamps","s":"Groups","u":"lamps/#groups","x":"Give lamps the same Group name to switch them together. Set Mood Lamp Group switches a group on or off, and Flicker Mood Lamps makes it flicker for a few seconds. Both work with or without a mood. A Mood Event can flicker, knock or switch a group when the play","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Lamps","s":"How the mood lights them","u":"lamps/#mood","x":"The mood sets every lamp's brightness and colour, measured from what it lights, so a lamp looks right in every mood. In Red Alert your lamps turn red and pulse. In Last Candle they dim to a warm, wavering glow and some go dark. With no mood, they shine at thei","k":"section"},{"p":"Lamp styles","s":"","u":"lamp-styles/","x":"The 8 lamp styles, and how to make your own with Customize This Style, with meshes of your own.","k":"page","i":"shapes"},{"p":"Lamp styles","s":"The 8 styles","u":"lamp-styles/#styles","x":"Style Colour Light Fixed Reach In a mood Hanging LS_Hanging 1, 0.82, 0.62 110° cone Hangs 10 m Follows the mood Bulb LS_Bulb 1, 0.78, 0.52 All round Hangs 8 m Follows the mood Wall LS_Wall 1, 0.84, 0.66 130° cone Wall 8 m Follows the mood Street LS_Street 1, 0","k":"section"},{"p":"Lamp styles","s":"Make your own style","u":"lamp-styles/#make-your-own-style","x":"Select a lamp of the style closest to what you want. Click Customize This Style on the Place tab, under Your own lamp styles . A copy is made in MoodKit > MyLampStyles , named like Hanging Custom , and the selected lamps take it in one undo. Change any value i","k":"section"},{"p":"Lamp styles","s":"Use your own meshes","u":"lamp-styles/#meshes","x":"Set the meshes of your style under Meshes . Sizes are in centimetres, for a mesh one metre across, and offsets are measured from the end of the stem. The stem is stretched to the stem length, so a stem mesh one metre long fits best. Keep Light Offset outside t","k":"section"},{"p":"Your level's lights","s":"","u":"level-lights/","x":"Tell Mood Kit what each of your lights is, see which lights a mood cannot change, and bring in lights added later.","k":"page","i":"bulb"},{"p":"Your level's lights","s":"What a light can be","u":"level-lights/#roles","x":"Follow mood Dims, tints and fails with the mood. The default. Never fails Follows the mood but never flickers or dies. Tag: MoodSteady Flame Flickers like fire and keeps its own warm colour. Tag: MoodFlame Alarm Pulses slowly, about once every 2 seconds. Tag: ","k":"section"},{"p":"Your level's lights","s":"Choose what a light does","u":"level-lights/#choose","x":"Select one or more lights in the level or the Outliner. Click a role under Lights on the Place tab. The status line says what changed, and the line under the buttons counts your lights. Roles undo like any edit. They are saved as actor tags, so you can also ty","k":"section"},{"p":"Your level's lights","s":"Lights a mood cannot change","u":"level-lights/#static","x":"Static lights and baked light cannot change while a game runs. A mood still changes the sky, fog, colour and exposure on a baked level, and the status line tells you how many lights it cannot change. When a level has static lights, a row at the bottom of the M","k":"section"},{"p":"Your level's lights","s":"Lights that stand in for daylight","u":"level-lights/#fill","x":"Environment packs often light a courtyard or a room with plain lights that have no lamp around them, to fake daylight or bounce. A mood treats a light with no lamp mesh near it, and no role, as one of these: it takes the colour of the mood's sky instead of the","k":"section"},{"p":"Your level's lights","s":"Lamp meshes","u":"level-lights/#meshes","x":"A lamp mesh is dimmed with its light when the mesh is small and close to the light, or in the same actor. A lamp mesh with no collision, in a separate actor, stays bright.","k":"section"},{"p":"Your level's lights","s":"Lights added later","u":"level-lights/#later","x":"A light you add in the editor joins the mood within a second. Levels that stream in later change their sky, fog and colour at once. Their lamps join when you call Refresh Mood Lights after the level has loaded.","k":"section"},{"p":"Your level's lights","s":"Pools of light a mood adds","u":"level-lights/#added","x":"Moods such as Failing Power, Red Alert and Long Dusk bring up to 4 pools of lamplight of their own, but only on levels with fewer than 3 lamps and no Mood Lamps. They stay ahead of the player. To never add them, untick Added lamps on the Fit tab.","k":"section"},{"p":"Apply and play","s":"","u":"apply-and-play/","x":"What Apply to Level does, how to remove a mood, the in-game mood picker and packaged games.","k":"page","i":"play"},{"p":"Apply and play","s":"Apply to Level","u":"apply-and-play/#apply","x":"Set up the mood on the three tabs. Click Apply to Level. The status line says what was applied and the card gets a small ON tag. A BP_MoodDirector actor appears in the Outliner. Save the level with Ctrl + S . Press Play. The mood starts with the game. An appli","k":"section"},{"p":"Apply and play","s":"Remove a mood","u":"apply-and-play/#remove","x":"Click Back to Original , then Apply to Level , or delete the BP_MoodDirector actor. The level looks as you built it, in the editor and in the game.","k":"section"},{"p":"Apply and play","s":"Change it on the actor","u":"apply-and-play/#details","x":"Select BP_MoodDirector to change its mood, weather, sliders, parts, sun aim and wind in the Details panel.","k":"section"},{"p":"Apply and play","s":"A preview never reaches the game","u":"apply-and-play/#preview","x":"A mood you only previewed, and never applied, stays out of the game. Play shows the level as it is saved.","k":"section"},{"p":"Apply and play","s":"The in-game mood picker","u":"apply-and-play/#demo","x":"Drag BP_MoodDemo into a level and press M while playing. The same gallery appears at the side of the game, with a mouse pointer. Moods blend in about 2 seconds. It is for showing moods, so it has no Apply button.","k":"section"},{"p":"Apply and play","s":"Packaged games","u":"apply-and-play/#packaging","x":"A packaged game only includes the moods and weathers something refers to. A mood or weather on an actor, a node or a Mood Event is included by itself, and so is the weather each mood comes with. For the in-game picker, add MoodKit/Moods to Additional Asset Dir","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Events and zones","s":"","u":"events-and-zones/","x":"Boxes that change things when the player walks in. Mood Events, Mood Zones and Weather Zones.","k":"page","i":"zone"},{"p":"Mood Events and zones","s":"Mood Events","u":"events-and-zones/#mood-events","x":"BP_MoodTrigger , the Mood Event, does what its tick boxes say when the player walks in. One box can do several things. Flicker a group of Mood Lamps for a few seconds, or switch them on or off. Knock hanging lamps so they swing and slowly settle. Start a black","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Events and zones","s":"Mood Event (BP_MoodTrigger)","u":"events-and-zones/#event-mood-event-bp-moodtrigger","x":"Value Range Default What it does Only Once switch ticked Happens only the first time the player walks in. Delay Seconds number 0 to 10 0 Waits this long after the player walks in. Group name empty Which Mood Lamps flicker or switch: those with this Group. Empt","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Events and zones","s":"Mood Zones","u":"events-and-zones/#mood-zones","x":"BP_MoodZone changes the mood while the player is inside it, and puts the earlier mood back as the player leaves.","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Events and zones","s":"Mood Zone (BP_MoodZone)","u":"events-and-zones/#zone-mood-zone-bp-moodzone","x":"Value Range Default What it does Mood mood asset empty The mood while the player is inside. Leave empty to return the level to its own look. Blend Seconds number 2 How long the change takes. Restore On Exit switch ticked Goes back to the earlier mood when the ","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Events and zones","s":"Weather Zones","u":"events-and-zones/#weather-zones","x":"BP_MoodWeatherZone changes the weather while the player is inside it. More in Storms and lightning .","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Events and zones","s":"Weather Zone (BP_MoodWeatherZone)","u":"events-and-zones/#wzone-weather-zone-bp-moodweatherzone","x":"Value Range Default What it does Weather weather asset empty The weather while the player is inside, such as WX_Snow or WX_Storm. Leave empty for the mood's own weather. Blend Seconds number 0 to 30 5 How long the change of weather takes. Restore On Exit switc","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood Events and zones","s":"In the Mood Lab","u":"events-and-zones/#lab","x":"BasementFlicker is a Mood Event in the basement. The two basement lamps flicker for 3 seconds and swing as if something knocked them. The candle keeps burning, because it has no group. StormCorner is a Weather Zone in a corner of the courtyard. A storm rolls i","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"","u":"blueprint-nodes/","x":"The 15 nodes under Mood Kit, drawn as they look in the graph, with what each one does.","k":"page","i":"node"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Example: a mood when the game starts","u":"blueprint-nodes/#example","x":"◆ Event BeginPlay f Set Mood Mood DA_BloodMoon Blend Seconds 2.0 Target is BPL Mood Kit Open the Level Blueprint. In the toolbar, click Blueprints , then Open Level Blueprint . Add Event BeginPlay if it is not there. Drag from its white arrow, type Set Mood an","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Change the mood","u":"blueprint-nodes/#mood","x":"f Set Mood Mood None Blend Seconds 2.0 Target is BPL Mood Kit Set Mood. Changes the mood of the level. Blend Seconds fades from the current look; 0 changes at once. f Clear Mood Blend Seconds 2.0 Target is BPL Mood Kit Clear Mood. Returns the level to how it w","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Fit it to the level","u":"blueprint-nodes/#fit","x":"f Set Mood Adjustments Brightness 0.0 Lights 0.0 Fog 1.0 Surface Wear 1.0 Target is BPL Mood Kit Set Mood Adjustments. Fits the mood to this level: Brightness and Lights in stops, Fog and Surface Wear as multipliers. f Set Mood Parts Sky Sun And Moon Light Bra","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Weather","u":"blueprint-nodes/#weather","x":"f Set Mood Weather Weather None Blend Seconds 5.0 Target is BPL Mood Kit Set Mood Weather. Puts a weather on the mood: rain, snow, ash or clear skies. Leave Weather empty for the mood's own. Blend Seconds fades it in, and the ground then soaks, dries or gather","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Lights","u":"blueprint-nodes/#lights","x":"f Trigger Blackout Seconds 3.0 Target is BPL Mood Kit Trigger Blackout. Cuts the lights for a few seconds, then brings them back. It needs a mood to be active. f Set Mood Lamp Group Group None On Target is BPL Mood Kit Set Mood Lamp Group. Switches every Mood ","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"","u":"mood-values/","x":"Every value of a mood, as it appears on a mood asset, with its range, default and what it does.","k":"page","i":"table"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Card","u":"mood-values/#mood-card","x":"Value Range Default What it does Display Name text empty The name on the card. Summary text empty One line about the mood, shown on the card and in the panel. Pack text Horror The pack this mood belongs to. Order whole number 100 Where the card sits in the gal","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sky","u":"mood-values/#mood-sky","x":"Value Range Default What it does Sun Elevation number 0 to 90 40 Height of the sun or moon above the horizon, in degrees. Sun Azimuth number -180 to 180 -25 Where the sun or moon stands, in degrees from the way the view faced when the mood began. 0 is straight","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog","u":"mood-values/#mood-fog","x":"Value Range Default What it does Fog Visibility Meters number 10 to 5000 3000 How far you can see through the fog, in metres. Fog Height Falloff number 0.001 to 2 0.2 How fast the fog thins with height. A low number keeps fog high in the air. Fog Max Opacity n","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cast Shadows","u":"mood-values/#mood-cast-shadows","x":"Value Range Default What it does Cast Clouds number 0 to 1 0 Shadows of passing clouds on the ground. Cast Cloud Scale number 10 to 200 70 Size of the cloud shadows, in metres. Cast Branches number 0 to 1 0 Shadows of branches, as if trees stood between the li","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Wear","u":"mood-values/#mood-surface-wear","x":"Value Range Default What it does Surface Wear number 0 to 1.5 1 How strongly all of the surface wear shows, with the wet ground and snow the weather leaves. 1 is as set here, 0 is none. It works like the Surface wear slider on the Fit tab. Surface Dirt number ","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Dust and Embers","u":"mood-values/#mood-dust-and-embers","x":"Value Range Default What it does Mote Amount number 0 to 1 0 How much dust or embers float in the air. Falling snow and ash come with the weather. Mote Size number 0.2 to 3 1 Size of each mote. Mote Fall number -0.5 to 1 0.02 How fast motes fall. Below 0 they ","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Weather","u":"mood-values/#mood-weather","x":"Value Range Default What it does Weather weather asset empty The weather this mood comes with: what falls, what it leaves on the ground, and the wind. Empty is clear. The panel and the Set Mood Weather node can put any other weather on the mood. Weather Rain n","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Lens","u":"mood-values/#mood-lens","x":"Value Range Default What it does Lens Tape number 0 to 1 0 Old video tape: lines, wobble and noise. Lens Edge number 0 to 1 0 Darkness that breathes at the corners of the frame. Lens Shimmer number 0 to 1 0 Heat shimmer over the whole picture. Lens Rain number","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Lamps and Exposure","u":"mood-values/#mood-lamps-and-exposure","x":"Value Range Default What it does Brightness number -3 to 3 0 Shifts the whole picture, in stops, like the Brightness slider on the Fit tab. Positive is brighter. Unlike Meter Bias, the lights keep their strength. Meter Bias number -6 to 3 0 Exposure of the who","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Added Lamps","u":"mood-values/#mood-added-lamps","x":"Value Range Default What it does Pool Key number 0 to 10 0 Brightness of the added lamps on the floor. 0 adds none. Pool Tint colour 1, 1, 1 Colour of the added lamps. Pool Cone Degrees number 10 to 120 50 Width of each added lamp's cone, in degrees. Pool Spac","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Player Light","u":"mood-values/#mood-player-light","x":"Value Range Default What it does Vision Key number 0 to 1 0 A faint glow around the player, so the floor near them shows. 0 is none. Vision Radius Meters number 1 to 30 8 How far the glow reaches, in metres. Vision Tint colour 1, 1, 1 Colour of the glow. Visio","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Picture","u":"mood-values/#mood-picture","x":"Value Range Default What it does Post Settings post process Colour grade, film curve, vignette, grain and bloom. The mood sets the exposure itself, so leave Exposure alone.","k":"section"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Display Name","u":"mood-values/#mood-DisplayName","x":"The name on the card.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Summary","u":"mood-values/#mood-Summary","x":"One line about the mood, shown on the card and in the panel.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pack","u":"mood-values/#mood-Pack","x":"The pack this mood belongs to.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Order","u":"mood-values/#mood-Order","x":"Where the card sits in the gallery. Lower comes first.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Thumbnail","u":"mood-values/#mood-Thumbnail","x":"The picture on the card.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sun Elevation","u":"mood-values/#mood-SunElevation","x":"Height of the sun or moon above the horizon, in degrees.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sun Azimuth","u":"mood-values/#mood-SunAzimuth","x":"Where the sun or moon stands, in degrees from the way the view faced when the mood began. 0 is straight ahead.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sun Key","u":"mood-values/#mood-SunKey","x":"Brightness of the sun or moon light on the ground. 0.18 makes a white wall in full light read middle grey.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sun Kelvin","u":"mood-values/#mood-SunKelvin","x":"Colour temperature of the sun or moon light. Low is orange, 6500 is white, high is blue.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sun Source Angle","u":"mood-values/#mood-SunSourceAngle","x":"Size of the light source in degrees. Bigger gives softer shadows.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sun Specular","u":"mood-values/#mood-SunSpecular","x":"How strongly the sun or moon shows in shiny surfaces.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sun Fog Scatter","u":"mood-values/#mood-SunFogScatter","x":"How much the sun or moon light lights up the fog.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sun Tint","u":"mood-values/#mood-SunTint","x":"Colour multiplied onto the sun or moon light.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sky Light Scale","u":"mood-values/#mood-SkyLightScale","x":"Strength of the soft light from the whole sky, which fills the shadows.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sky Light Tint","u":"mood-values/#mood-SkyLightTint","x":"Colour of the sky light.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sky Fog Scatter","u":"mood-values/#mood-SkyFogScatter","x":"How much the sky light lights up the fog.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sky Zenith","u":"mood-values/#mood-SkyZenith","x":"Colour of the sky straight up.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sky Horizon","u":"mood-values/#mood-SkyHorizon","x":"Colour of the sky at the horizon.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Sky Glow","u":"mood-values/#mood-SkyGlow","x":"Colour of the glow around the sun or moon.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Horizon Band","u":"mood-values/#mood-HorizonBand","x":"Strength of the bright band along the horizon under a low sun.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Moon Size","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoonSize","x":"Size of the moon disc. 0 shows no moon.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Moon Halo","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoonHalo","x":"Strength of the halo around the moon.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Moon Color","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoonColor","x":"Colour and brightness of the moon disc.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Star Amount","u":"mood-values/#mood-StarAmount","x":"How many stars show. 0 shows none.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cloud Cover","u":"mood-values/#mood-CloudCover","x":"How much of the sky the clouds cover.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cloud Soft","u":"mood-values/#mood-CloudSoft","x":"How soft the cloud edges are.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cloud Scale","u":"mood-values/#mood-CloudScale","x":"Size of the cloud shapes. A smaller number makes bigger clouds.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cloud Speed","u":"mood-values/#mood-CloudSpeed","x":"How fast the clouds move with the wind.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cloud Absorb","u":"mood-values/#mood-CloudAbsorb","x":"How dark thick clouds get.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cloud Lit","u":"mood-values/#mood-CloudLit","x":"Colour of the lit side of the clouds.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cloud Dark","u":"mood-values/#mood-CloudDark","x":"Colour of the shaded side of the clouds.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Visibility Meters","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogVisibilityMeters","x":"How far you can see through the fog, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Height Falloff","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogHeightFalloff","x":"How fast the fog thins with height. A low number keeps fog high in the air.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Max Opacity","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogMaxOpacity","x":"The most the fog can hide. 1 can hide everything far away.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Color","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogColor","x":"Colour of the fog.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Volumetric","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogVolumetric","x":"Lets lights shine through the fog in beams. It costs some speed.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Volumetric Extinction","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogVolumetricExtinction","x":"How much the beam fog blocks light.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Volumetric Distance Meters","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogVolumetricDistanceMeters","x":"How far from the view the beam fog reaches, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Volumetric Anisotropy","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogVolumetricAnisotropy","x":"How much the beam fog glows toward a light you look at. 0 glows evenly.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Volumetric Albedo","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogVolumetricAlbedo","x":"Colour of the beam fog.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Volumetric Glow","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogVolumetricGlow","x":"Light the beam fog gives off by itself.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Glow No Lumen","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogGlowNoLumen","x":"Extra glow for the beam fog in projects without Lumen.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Flare Color","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogFlareColor","x":"Colour of the fog toward the sun or moon.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Fog Flare Exponent","u":"mood-values/#mood-FogFlareExponent","x":"How tight the glow toward the sun or moon is.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Bank Density","u":"mood-values/#mood-BankDensity","x":"Thickness of the low fog bank. 0 is none.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Bank Top","u":"mood-values/#mood-BankTop","x":"Height of the top of the fog bank, in metres above the floor.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Bank Scale","u":"mood-values/#mood-BankScale","x":"Size of the shapes in the fog bank, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Bank Breakup","u":"mood-values/#mood-BankBreakup","x":"How patchy the fog bank is. 0 is even.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Bank Speed","u":"mood-values/#mood-BankSpeed","x":"How fast the fog bank drifts with the wind.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Bank Color","u":"mood-values/#mood-BankColor","x":"Colour of the fog bank.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Bank Glow","u":"mood-values/#mood-BankGlow","x":"Light the fog bank gives off by itself.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cast Clouds","u":"mood-values/#mood-CastClouds","x":"Shadows of passing clouds on the ground.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cast Cloud Scale","u":"mood-values/#mood-CastCloudScale","x":"Size of the cloud shadows, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cast Branches","u":"mood-values/#mood-CastBranches","x":"Shadows of branches, as if trees stood between the light and the level.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cast Leaves","u":"mood-values/#mood-CastLeaves","x":"Shadows of leaves.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cast Branch Scale","u":"mood-values/#mood-CastBranchScale","x":"Size of the branch and leaf shadows, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cast Sway","u":"mood-values/#mood-CastSway","x":"How much the branches sway in the wind.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cast Soft","u":"mood-values/#mood-CastSoft","x":"How blurred the branch shadows are.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cast Blinds","u":"mood-values/#mood-CastBlinds","x":"Shadows of window blinds: bars of light and shade wherever the sun or moon falls, as if it shone through slats.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cast Blind Scale","u":"mood-values/#mood-CastBlindScale","x":"Distance between the bars of the blinds, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Wear","u":"mood-values/#mood-SurfaceWear","x":"How strongly all of the surface wear shows, with the wet ground and snow the weather leaves. 1 is as set here, 0 is none. It works like the Surface wear slider on the Fit tab.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Dirt","u":"mood-values/#mood-SurfaceDirt","x":"Dirt in patches on every surface.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Stain","u":"mood-values/#mood-SurfaceStain","x":"Rust or stains, in the stain colour.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Streaks","u":"mood-values/#mood-SurfaceStreaks","x":"Dark streaks running down walls.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Cracks","u":"mood-values/#mood-SurfaceCracks","x":"Thin dark cracks.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Damp","u":"mood-values/#mood-SurfaceDamp","x":"Damp climbing up from the bottom of walls.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Damp Height","u":"mood-values/#mood-SurfaceDampHeight","x":"How high the damp climbs, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Wet","u":"mood-values/#mood-SurfaceWet","x":"Wet, glossy floors, whatever the weather. Rain makes them wetter while it lasts.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Puddles","u":"mood-values/#mood-SurfacePuddles","x":"Standing water where floors dip, whatever the weather.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Cover","u":"mood-values/#mood-SurfaceCover","x":"Dust or old ash lying on what faces up, whatever the weather. Snow and ash that fall settle by themselves.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cover Indoors","u":"mood-values/#mood-CoverIndoors","x":"How much of the cover also lies inside interior volumes. 0 keeps it outside.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Surface Bump","u":"mood-values/#mood-SurfaceBump","x":"Fine relief on every surface, so light has something to catch on.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Dirt Color","u":"mood-values/#mood-DirtColor","x":"Colour of dirt, streaks and damp.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Stain Color","u":"mood-values/#mood-StainColor","x":"Colour of stains.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Cover Color","u":"mood-values/#mood-CoverColor","x":"Colour of the cover.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Mote Amount","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoteAmount","x":"How much dust or embers float in the air. Falling snow and ash come with the weather.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Mote Size","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoteSize","x":"Size of each mote.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Mote Fall","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoteFall","x":"How fast motes fall. Below 0 they rise.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Mote Drift","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoteDrift","x":"How fast motes drift with the wind.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Mote Ember","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoteEmber","x":"How many motes glow like embers.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Mote Flake","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoteFlake","x":"Makes motes flat flakes that tumble.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Mote Shade","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoteShade","x":"How much motes darken what is behind them.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Mote Indoors","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoteIndoors","x":"How many motes also float inside interior volumes. 0 keeps them outside.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Mote Color","u":"mood-values/#mood-MoteColor","x":"Colour of the motes.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Weather","u":"mood-values/#mood-Weather","x":"The weather this mood comes with: what falls, what it leaves on the ground, and the wind. Empty is clear. The panel and the Set Mood Weather node can put any other weather on the mood.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Weather Rain","u":"mood-values/#mood-WeatherRain","x":"Scales the weather's rain, its marks on the ground and its drops on the lens. 1 is as the weather has it, 0 is none.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Weather Flakes","u":"mood-values/#mood-WeatherFlakes","x":"Scales the weather's falling snow and ash, and how much of it settles. 1 is as the weather has it, 0 is none.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Weather Lightning","u":"mood-values/#mood-WeatherLightning","x":"Scales how often the weather's lightning strikes. 1 is as the weather has it, 0 is none.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Weather Wind","u":"mood-values/#mood-WeatherWind","x":"Scales the strength of the weather's wind. 1 is as the weather has it, 0 is still air.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Lens Tape","u":"mood-values/#mood-LensTape","x":"Old video tape: lines, wobble and noise.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Lens Edge","u":"mood-values/#mood-LensEdge","x":"Darkness that breathes at the corners of the frame.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Lens Shimmer","u":"mood-values/#mood-LensShimmer","x":"Heat shimmer over the whole picture.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Lens Rain","u":"mood-values/#mood-LensRain","x":"How much of the weather's rain on the lens shows. 1 is all of it, 0 is none.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Brightness","u":"mood-values/#mood-Brightness","x":"Shifts the whole picture, in stops, like the Brightness slider on the Fit tab. Positive is brighter. Unlike Meter Bias, the lights keep their strength.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Meter Bias","u":"mood-values/#mood-MeterBias","x":"Exposure of the whole mood, in stops, on top of what the level measures. Lower is darker.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Light Gain Stops","u":"mood-values/#mood-LightGainStops","x":"Brightness of the level's own lamps, in stops.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Light Tint","u":"mood-values/#mood-LightTint","x":"Colour multiplied onto the level's lamps. Lamps marked Flame or Alarm keep their own colour.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Light Dead Fraction","u":"mood-values/#mood-LightDeadFraction","x":"Share of the level's lamps that stay dead. Lamps marked Never Fails, Flame, Alarm or Faulty never die.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Light Failures Per Minute","u":"mood-values/#mood-LightFailuresPerMinute","x":"How often a lamp stutters, per minute. One lamp at a time, never faster than 2.5 flashes a second.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Light Pulse Hz","u":"mood-values/#mood-LightPulseHz","x":"A slow alarm pulse on every lamp, in pulses per second. It stays under the safe limit for flashing light.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Light Pulse Depth","u":"mood-values/#mood-LightPulseDepth","x":"How deep the pulse goes. 1 goes fully dark.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Light Flame Amount","u":"mood-values/#mood-LightFlameAmount","x":"Flame flicker on every lamp.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Light Fog Glow","u":"mood-values/#mood-LightFogGlow","x":"How much the lamps light up the fog.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Light Tint B","u":"mood-values/#mood-LightTintB","x":"A second colour for some of the level's lamps, for two-colour looks such as neon.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Light Tint Split","u":"mood-values/#mood-LightTintSplit","x":"Share of the level's lamps that take the second colour. 0 is none.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Adapt Stops","u":"mood-values/#mood-AdaptStops","x":"How far the exposure may rise, in stops, where the level hides the mood's light, such as under thick trees or in closed rooms. 0 keeps the mood exactly as dark as it falls.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool Key","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolKey","x":"Brightness of the added lamps on the floor. 0 adds none.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool Tint","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolTint","x":"Colour of the added lamps.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool Cone Degrees","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolConeDegrees","x":"Width of each added lamp's cone, in degrees.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool Spacing Meters","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolSpacingMeters","x":"Distance between added lamps, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool Height Meters","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolHeightMeters","x":"Height of the added lamps in the open, in metres. Under a roof they hang from it.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool Flicker","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolFlicker","x":"How much the added lamps flicker, and whether some of them are dead.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool Sweep Hz","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolSweepHz","x":"Turns the added lamps like beacons, in turns per second.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool Fog Scatter","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolFogScatter","x":"How much the added lamps light up the fog.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool Tint B","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolTintB","x":"A second colour for some of the added lamps.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool Tint Split","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolTintSplit","x":"Share of the added lamps that take the second colour. 0 is none.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool From Below","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolFromBelow","x":"Puts the added lamps on the floor, shining up, so walls and faces are lit from below. 0 hangs them overhead. Height then sets how far their light reaches.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Pool Always","u":"mood-values/#mood-PoolAlways","x":"Adds the lamps on every level. 0 adds them only to levels with fewer than three lamps and no Mood Lamps. For moods whose look is the added light itself, such as lamps on the floor.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Vision Key","u":"mood-values/#mood-VisionKey","x":"A faint glow around the player, so the floor near them shows. 0 is none.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Vision Radius Meters","u":"mood-values/#mood-VisionRadiusMeters","x":"How far the glow reaches, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Vision Tint","u":"mood-values/#mood-VisionTint","x":"Colour of the glow.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Vision Flame","u":"mood-values/#mood-VisionFlame","x":"Makes the glow flicker like a candle the player carries.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Beam Key","u":"mood-values/#mood-BeamKey","x":"Brightness of the torch the player carries. 0 is none.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Beam Tint","u":"mood-values/#mood-BeamTint","x":"Colour of the torch.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Beam Cone Degrees","u":"mood-values/#mood-BeamConeDegrees","x":"Width of the torch beam, in degrees.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Beam Range Meters","u":"mood-values/#mood-BeamRangeMeters","x":"How far the torch reaches, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Beam Flash Seconds","u":"mood-values/#mood-BeamFlashSeconds","x":"Turns the torch into a camera flash that fires every this many seconds. 0 keeps a steady torch. It never fires more often than once every 3 seconds, well under the limit for flashing light.","k":"value"},{"p":"Mood values","s":"Post Settings","u":"mood-values/#mood-PostSettings","x":"Colour grade, film curve, vignette, grain and bloom. The mood sets the exposure itself, so leave Exposure alone.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"","u":"weather-values/","x":"Every value of a weather asset, and the nine weathers side by side.","k":"page","i":"table"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"The weathers side by side","u":"weather-values/#compare","x":"Value Clear Drizzle Rain Storm Dry Lightning Snow Blizzard Ash Light Ash Rain RainAmount 0 0.22 0.55 0.9 0 0 0 0 0 Snow and ash FlakeAmount 0 0 0 0 0 0.32 0.85 0.24 0.2 Wet ground GroundWet 0 0.55 0.92 1 0 0 0 0 0 Puddles GroundPuddles 0 0.1 0.6 0.8 0 0 0 0 0 ","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Every value","u":"weather-values/#values","x":"","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Card","u":"weather-values/#weather-card","x":"Value Range Default What it does Display Name text empty The name in the panel. Summary text empty One line about the weather, shown in the panel. Order whole number 100 Where it sits in the list. Lower comes first.","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Rain","u":"weather-values/#weather-rain","x":"Value Range Default What it does Rain Amount number 0 to 1 0 How hard it rains. Rain stays out of interior volumes. Rain Length number 0.1 to 1 0.5 Length of the rain streaks. Rain Color colour 0.6, 0.7, 0.8 Colour of the rain. Lens Rain number 0 to 1 0 Rain d","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Snow and Ash","u":"weather-values/#weather-snow-and-ash","x":"Value Range Default What it does Flake Amount number 0 to 1 0 How much snow or ash falls. Flake Size number 0.2 to 3 1 Size of each flake. Flake Fall number 0 to 3 0.8 How fast flakes fall, in metres a second. Flake Drift number 0 to 2 0.5 How much the wind ca","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Ground","u":"weather-values/#weather-ground","x":"Value Range Default What it does Ground Wet number 0 to 1 0 How wet floors get while this weather lasts. Ground Puddles number 0 to 1 0 How much standing water gathers. Ground Ripples number 0 to 1 0 Rain rings in puddles, and wet walls. They stay out of inter","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Build Up","u":"weather-values/#weather-build-up","x":"Value Range Default What it does Soak Seconds number 1 to 600 60 In a game, how long dry ground takes to get as wet as this weather makes it. Dry Seconds number 1 to 900 240 In a game, how long ground that is wetter than this weather leaves it takes to dry. Se","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Lightning","u":"weather-values/#weather-lightning","x":"Value Range Default What it does Lightning Per Minute number 0 to 20 0 How many strikes a minute, on average. 0 is none. Strikes are always at least 4 seconds apart, and each flashes at most 3 times. Lightning Brightness number 0 to 4 1 How brightly a strike l","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Wind","u":"weather-values/#weather-wind","x":"Value Range Default What it does Wind Strength number 0 to 3 1 How strong the wind is. 1 is a breeze, 3 a gale. Clouds, fog, rain, snow, branch shadows and swinging lamps all follow it. Wind Gusts number 0 to 1 0.2 How much the wind comes and goes in gusts.","k":"section"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Display Name","u":"weather-values/#weather-DisplayName","x":"The name in the panel.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Summary","u":"weather-values/#weather-Summary","x":"One line about the weather, shown in the panel.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Order","u":"weather-values/#weather-Order","x":"Where it sits in the list. Lower comes first.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Rain Amount","u":"weather-values/#weather-RainAmount","x":"How hard it rains. Rain stays out of interior volumes.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Rain Length","u":"weather-values/#weather-RainLength","x":"Length of the rain streaks.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Rain Color","u":"weather-values/#weather-RainColor","x":"Colour of the rain.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Lens Rain","u":"weather-values/#weather-LensRain","x":"Rain drops running down the lens. They stop while the view is inside an interior volume.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Flake Amount","u":"weather-values/#weather-FlakeAmount","x":"How much snow or ash falls.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Flake Size","u":"weather-values/#weather-FlakeSize","x":"Size of each flake.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Flake Fall","u":"weather-values/#weather-FlakeFall","x":"How fast flakes fall, in metres a second.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Flake Drift","u":"weather-values/#weather-FlakeDrift","x":"How much the wind carries the flakes sideways.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Flake Swirl","u":"weather-values/#weather-FlakeSwirl","x":"How far each flake wanders and circles on its way down.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Flake Tumble","u":"weather-values/#weather-FlakeTumble","x":"0 gives soft round flakes, like snow. 1 gives flat flakes that turn over as they fall, like ash.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Flake Shade","u":"weather-values/#weather-FlakeShade","x":"How much flakes darken what is behind them. Ash darkens it, snow hardly does.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Flake Color","u":"weather-values/#weather-FlakeColor","x":"Colour of the flakes.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Flake Indoors","u":"weather-values/#weather-FlakeIndoors","x":"How much also falls and settles inside interior volumes. 0 keeps it all outside.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Ground Wet","u":"weather-values/#weather-GroundWet","x":"How wet floors get while this weather lasts.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Ground Puddles","u":"weather-values/#weather-GroundPuddles","x":"How much standing water gathers.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Ground Ripples","u":"weather-values/#weather-GroundRipples","x":"Rain rings in puddles, and wet walls. They stay out of interior volumes.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Ground Cover","u":"weather-values/#weather-GroundCover","x":"How much snow or ash settles on everything that faces up.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Cover Color","u":"weather-values/#weather-CoverColor","x":"Colour of the snow or ash that settles.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Soak Seconds","u":"weather-values/#weather-SoakSeconds","x":"In a game, how long dry ground takes to get as wet as this weather makes it.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Dry Seconds","u":"weather-values/#weather-DrySeconds","x":"In a game, how long ground that is wetter than this weather leaves it takes to dry.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Settle Seconds","u":"weather-values/#weather-SettleSeconds","x":"In a game, how long snow or ash takes to settle as thick as this weather leaves it.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Melt Seconds","u":"weather-values/#weather-MeltSeconds","x":"In a game, how long settled snow or ash takes to go when this weather has less of it.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Lightning Per Minute","u":"weather-values/#weather-LightningPerMinute","x":"How many strikes a minute, on average. 0 is none. Strikes are always at least 4 seconds apart, and each flashes at most 3 times.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Lightning Brightness","u":"weather-values/#weather-LightningBrightness","x":"How brightly a strike lights the level and the sky.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Lightning Bolt","u":"weather-values/#weather-LightningBolt","x":"How often the bolt itself shows in the sky. The other strikes light the clouds from behind.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Lightning Color","u":"weather-values/#weather-LightningColor","x":"Colour of the lightning.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Wind Strength","u":"weather-values/#weather-WindStrength","x":"How strong the wind is. 1 is a breeze, 3 a gale. Clouds, fog, rain, snow, branch shadows and swinging lamps all follow it.","k":"value"},{"p":"Weather values","s":"Wind Gusts","u":"weather-values/#weather-WindGusts","x":"How much the wind comes and goes in gusts.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"","u":"lamp-values/","x":"The settings on each placed Mood Lamp, and every value of a lamp style.","k":"page","i":"table"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Mood Lamp, on each placed lamp","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-mood-lamp-on-each-placed-lamp","x":"Value Range Default What it does Style lamp style asset How the lamp looks and shines. Pick any Lamp Style, or make your own with Customize This Style on the Place tab. Brightness number 0 to 4 1 Multiplies how bright the lamp is, with or without a mood. Colou","k":"section"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Lamp style: Style","u":"lamp-values/#style-lamp-style-style","x":"Value Range Default What it does Display Name text empty The name of this style.","k":"section"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Lamp style: Light","u":"lamp-values/#style-lamp-style-light","x":"Value Range Default What it does All Round switch unticked Shines all round, like a bare bulb or a flame. Off shines a cone, like a shaded lamp. Cone Degrees number 10 to 160 110 How wide the cone of light is, in degrees. Aim Pitch number -90 to 90 -90 Where t","k":"section"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Lamp style: Placing","u":"lamp-values/#style-lamp-style-placing","x":"Value Range Default What it does Hangs Down switch ticked Hangs from the ceiling on its stem. On Wall switch unticked Fixed to a wall, with its stem pointing out. With neither, it stands on the floor or a table. Stem Meters number 0 to 12 0.7 The length of the","k":"section"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Lamp style: Meshes","u":"lamp-values/#style-lamp-style-meshes","x":"Value Range Default What it does Stem Mesh static mesh Cylinder The cable, arm or pole. It is stretched to the stem length, so a mesh one metre long fits best. Body Mesh static mesh Cone The shade, housing or candle. Body Size x, y, z 46, 46, 26 The size of th","k":"section"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Style","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-Style","x":"How the lamp looks and shines. Pick any Lamp Style, or make your own with Customize This Style on the Place tab.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Brightness","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-Brightness","x":"Multiplies how bright the lamp is, with or without a mood.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Colour","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-Colour","x":"Multiplies the style's colour. White keeps it.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Reach","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-Reach","x":"Multiplies how far the light reaches.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Cone Degrees","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-ConeDegrees","x":"How wide the cone of light is. 0 keeps the style's cone.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Stem Meters","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-StemMeters","x":"The length of the cable, arm or pole, in metres. 0 keeps the style's length.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Cast Shadows","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-CastShadows","x":"The light casts shadows. Off is cheaper when there are many lamps.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Show Fixture","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-ShowFixture","x":"Shows the lamp itself. Off leaves only the light, for a lamp mesh of your own.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Fog Glow","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-FogGlow","x":"Multiplies how strongly its light shows in fog.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Sway Degrees","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-SwayDegrees","x":"How far a hanging lamp swings either way, in degrees. 0 keeps it still. It swings in the game, and in the editor while a mood is previewed. Outside an interior volume it swings along the wind, further in a strong wind.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Sway Seconds","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-SwaySeconds","x":"How long one swing of a hanging lamp takes, in seconds.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Group","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-Group","x":"A name for switching lamps together. A Mood Event or the Set Mood Lamp Group node switches every lamp with this group.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Starts Off","u":"lamp-values/#lamp-StartsOff","x":"The lamp starts switched off, until a Mood Event or Set Mood Lamp Group switches it on.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Display Name","u":"lamp-values/#style-DisplayName","x":"The name of this style.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"All Round","u":"lamp-values/#style-AllRound","x":"Shines all round, like a bare bulb or a flame. Off shines a cone, like a shaded lamp.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Cone Degrees","u":"lamp-values/#style-ConeDegrees","x":"How wide the cone of light is, in degrees.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Aim Pitch","u":"lamp-values/#style-AimPitch","x":"Where the cone points: -90 is straight down, 0 is straight ahead.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Key","u":"lamp-values/#style-Key","x":"How brightly the lamp lights what is in front of it while a mood runs. 1 is a soft pool, 3 a bright one. The mood dims or brightens it further.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Editor Candela","u":"lamp-values/#style-EditorCandela","x":"How bright the lamp is when no mood is on, in candelas.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Reach Meters","u":"lamp-values/#style-ReachMeters","x":"How far its light reaches, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Colour","u":"lamp-values/#style-Colour","x":"The colour of its light.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Soft Shadows","u":"lamp-values/#style-SoftShadows","x":"The size of the light source in centimetres. Bigger gives softer shadows.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Fog Glow","u":"lamp-values/#style-FogGlow","x":"How strongly its light shows in fog.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Is Flame","u":"lamp-values/#style-IsFlame","x":"Flickers like a flame and keeps its own colour in every mood, unless its role is set otherwise.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Is Alarm","u":"lamp-values/#style-IsAlarm","x":"Pulses like an alarm and keeps its own colour in every mood, unless its role is set otherwise.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Hangs Down","u":"lamp-values/#style-HangsDown","x":"Hangs from the ceiling on its stem.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"On Wall","u":"lamp-values/#style-OnWall","x":"Fixed to a wall, with its stem pointing out. With neither, it stands on the floor or a table.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Stem Meters","u":"lamp-values/#style-StemMeters","x":"The length of the cable, arm or pole, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Stem Width","u":"lamp-values/#style-StemWidth","x":"The thickness of the cable, arm or pole, in centimetres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Stem Mesh","u":"lamp-values/#style-StemMesh","x":"The cable, arm or pole. It is stretched to the stem length, so a mesh one metre long fits best.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Body Mesh","u":"lamp-values/#style-BodyMesh","x":"The shade, housing or candle.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Body Size","u":"lamp-values/#style-BodySize","x":"The size of the body, in centimetres, for a mesh one metre across.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Body Offset","u":"lamp-values/#style-BodyOffset","x":"Where the body sits, from the end of the stem.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Body Colour","u":"lamp-values/#style-BodyColour","x":"The colour of the body and the stem.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Glow Mesh","u":"lamp-values/#style-GlowMesh","x":"The bulb, flame or glass that glows.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Glow Size","u":"lamp-values/#style-GlowSize","x":"The size of the glowing part, in centimetres, for a mesh one metre across.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Glow Offset","u":"lamp-values/#style-GlowOffset","x":"Where the glowing part sits, from the end of the stem.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Glow Strength","u":"lamp-values/#style-GlowStrength","x":"How bright the glowing part looks.","k":"value"},{"p":"Lamp values","s":"Light Offset","u":"lamp-values/#style-LightOffset","x":"Where the light itself sits, from the end of the stem. Keep it outside the body, or the body blocks it.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"","u":"event-values/","x":"The settings of Mood Events, Mood Zones, Weather Zones and interior volumes.","k":"page","i":"table"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Mood Event (BP_MoodTrigger)","u":"event-values/#event-mood-event-bp-moodtrigger","x":"Value Range Default What it does Only Once switch ticked Happens only the first time the player walks in. Delay Seconds number 0 to 10 0 Waits this long after the player walks in. Group name empty Which Mood Lamps flicker or switch: those with this Group. Empt","k":"section"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Mood Zone (BP_MoodZone)","u":"event-values/#zone-mood-zone-bp-moodzone","x":"Value Range Default What it does Mood mood asset empty The mood while the player is inside. Leave empty to return the level to its own look. Blend Seconds number 2 How long the change takes. Restore On Exit switch ticked Goes back to the earlier mood when the ","k":"section"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Weather Zone (BP_MoodWeatherZone)","u":"event-values/#wzone-weather-zone-bp-moodweatherzone","x":"Value Range Default What it does Weather weather asset empty The weather while the player is inside, such as WX_Snow or WX_Storm. Leave empty for the mood's own weather. Blend Seconds number 0 to 30 5 How long the change of weather takes. Restore On Exit switc","k":"section"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Interior volume (BP_MoodInterior)","u":"event-values/#room-interior-volume-bp-moodinterior","x":"Value Range Default What it does Brightness number -3 to 3 0 Shifts the exposure while the view is inside, in stops. Positive is brighter, as eyes adjust to a dark room. Fog Amount number 0 to 2 1 Multiplies the height fog while the view is inside. 1 is as the","k":"section"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Only Once","u":"event-values/#event-OnlyOnce","x":"Happens only the first time the player walks in.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Delay Seconds","u":"event-values/#event-DelaySeconds","x":"Waits this long after the player walks in.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Group","u":"event-values/#event-Group","x":"Which Mood Lamps flicker or switch: those with this Group. Empty means every Mood Lamp.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Flicker Seconds","u":"event-values/#event-FlickerSeconds","x":"The lamps flicker for this long. 0 is no flicker.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Swing Degrees","u":"event-values/#event-SwingDegrees","x":"Hanging lamps of the group swing this far, as if something knocked them, then slowly settle. 0 is no swing.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Switch Lamps","u":"event-values/#event-SwitchLamps","x":"Switches the lamps on or off. With Flicker too, they flicker first.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Lamps On","u":"event-values/#event-LampsOn","x":"With Switch Lamps: on is ticked, off is unticked.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Blackout","u":"event-values/#event-Blackout","x":"Cuts the lights that follow the mood. Flame and Alarm lamps stay on.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Blackout Seconds","u":"event-values/#event-BlackoutSeconds","x":"How long the blackout lasts.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Lightning","u":"event-values/#event-Lightning","x":"Strikes lightning as the player walks in, in any weather.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"New Mood","u":"event-values/#event-NewMood","x":"Changes to this mood. Leave empty to keep the mood.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Mood Seconds","u":"event-values/#event-MoodSeconds","x":"How long the change of mood takes.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"New Weather","u":"event-values/#event-NewWeather","x":"Changes the weather to this one, such as rain or snow. Leave empty to keep the weather.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Weather Seconds","u":"event-values/#event-WeatherSeconds","x":"How long the change of weather takes. The ground goes on soaking, drying or gathering snow for longer, at the pace the weather sets.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Mood","u":"event-values/#zone-Mood","x":"The mood while the player is inside. Leave empty to return the level to its own look.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Blend Seconds","u":"event-values/#zone-BlendSeconds","x":"How long the change takes.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Restore On Exit","u":"event-values/#zone-RestoreOnExit","x":"Goes back to the earlier mood when the player leaves.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Weather","u":"event-values/#wzone-Weather","x":"The weather while the player is inside, such as WX_Snow or WX_Storm. Leave empty for the mood's own weather.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Blend Seconds","u":"event-values/#wzone-BlendSeconds","x":"How long the change of weather takes.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Restore On Exit","u":"event-values/#wzone-RestoreOnExit","x":"Goes back to the earlier weather when the player leaves.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Ground At Once","u":"event-values/#wzone-GroundAtOnce","x":"The ground takes this weather's look at once, as if it had always been here, instead of soaking or turning white over time.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Brightness","u":"event-values/#room-Brightness","x":"Shifts the exposure while the view is inside, in stops. Positive is brighter, as eyes adjust to a dark room.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Fog Amount","u":"event-values/#room-FogAmount","x":"Multiplies the height fog while the view is inside. 1 is as the mood has it, 0 is clear air.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Keep Rain Out","u":"event-values/#room-KeepRainOut","x":"No rain, rain marks, lens drops, or falling ash and snow inside. Dust in the air stays.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Keep Fog Bank Out","u":"event-values/#room-KeepFogBankOut","x":"No low fog bank inside.","k":"value"},{"p":"Event and zone values","s":"Blend Meters","u":"event-values/#room-BlendMeters","x":"How far the change in brightness and fog spreads either side of the walls, in metres.","k":"value"},{"p":"Limits and tips","s":"","u":"limits/","x":"What a mood cannot do, and the behaviour that is on purpose.","k":"page","i":"info"},{"p":"Limits and tips","s":"What a mood cannot do","u":"limits/#cannot","x":"Static and baked lights cannot change at runtime. A mood still changes the sky, fog, colour and exposure on a baked level. The panel tells you how many lights it cannot change, and offers Make Lights Movable and Build Lighting . A camera with its own post proc","k":"section"},{"p":"Limits and tips","s":"On purpose","u":"limits/#on-purpose","x":"Characters stay clean. Surface wear leaves characters out, so dirt does not slide across them. Lightning indoors. A strike lights a room only through its doors and windows, because its light casts shadows. Lightning with your own sky. With Sky unticked, a stri","k":"section"},{"p":"Limits and tips","s":"With your own sky, fog or meshes","u":"limits/#yours","x":"A sky Blueprint from another pack counts as a sky, because it holds a sky and its lights in one actor. Untick Sky to keep it. The fog bank with your own height fog. The fog bank needs the mood's height fog. With Height fog unticked, the fog bank only shows if ","k":"section"},{"p":"Limits and tips","s":"Keep it fast","u":"limits/#fast","x":"Each Mood Lamp is a real light with shadows. Untick Cast Shadows on lamps far from the player. Untick any part you do not need on the Fit tab, and your level keeps its own version of it. Pools of light a mood adds only appear on levels with fewer than 3 lamps ","k":"section"},{"p":"Questions","s":"","u":"faq/","x":"Answers to the questions people ask most, from the first open to packaged games.","k":"page","i":"help"},{"p":"Questions","s":"Getting going","u":"faq/#start","x":"The first mood I click looks grey or plain. Unreal prepares the materials the first time it sees them, which can take up to a minute. It only happens once. Wait, and the mood appears. The Mood Kit button is not in the toolbar. A pack from Fab cannot add a butt","k":"section"},{"p":"Questions","s":"Looks","u":"faq/#looks","x":"Rain falls inside my building. Mood Kit cannot know where your roofs are. Put an interior volume around each indoor space with Add Interior Volume on the Place tab. See Indoor rooms . My lights do not change with the mood. Static lights and baked light cannot ","k":"section"},{"p":"Questions","s":"Your work","u":"faq/#your-work","x":"Will an update overwrite my own moods? No. Your moods, lamp styles and weathers live in MyMoods , MyLampStyles and MyWeather , apart from the pack, and an update never touches them. How do I remove a mood from my level? Click Back to Original , then Apply to L","k":"section"},{"p":"Questions","s":"In the game","u":"faq/#game","x":"My Mood Event does nothing in the editor. Mood Events only fire in the game, when the player walks in. Press Play and walk into the box. My packaged game is missing some moods. A packaged game only includes moods and weathers something refers to. For the in-ga","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"","u":"support/","x":"Fix common problems in a minute, or send a ready-made report on Discord or by email. Also the engine versions Mood Kit works with, and credits.","k":"page","i":"mail"},{"p":"Support","s":"How to get help fast","u":"support/#how","x":"1 Find your problem . Type a few words in the box below. Most fixes take a minute. 2 Try it in the Mood Lab. Open it from Content > MoodKit > Levels . If it works there, the difference is in your level, and that helps to find it. 3 Send a report . Fill in the ","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Fix it yourself","u":"support/#fixes","x":"Click a problem to see its fix, or type a few words to find yours.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Send a report","u":"support/#report","x":"Fill in what you can. Your report is written as you type, ready to paste on Discord or send by email.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Add a screenshot","u":"support/#screenshot","x":"Take a screenshot of the view with the Mood Gallery open, and keep its status line in the picture. Status line The status line is the last line of the Mood Gallery. It counts the lights a mood can change and the static lights it cannot.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Works with","u":"support/#versions","x":"Made in Unreal Engine 5.2, so it opens in 5.2 and newer . Blueprint only. Nothing to compile. No plugins to turn on. Works with Lumen on or off .","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Credits","u":"support/#credits","x":"All textures are generated by code, and the Mood Lab level is made for this pack.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"The first mood I click looks grey or plain","u":"support/#fix-the-first-mood-i-click-looks-grey-or-plain","x":"Unreal prepares the materials the first time it sees them, which can take up to a minute. It only happens once. Wait, and the mood appears.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"The Mood Kit button is not in the toolbar","u":"support/#fix-the-mood-kit-button-is-not-in-the-toolbar","x":"A pack from Fab cannot add a button by itself. The first time, right-click EUW_MoodGallery in Content > MoodKit and choose Run Editor Utility Widget . If the button is missing after a restart, open Tools > Mood Gallery once and it is back.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"I cannot find the Set Mood node","u":"support/#fix-i-cannot-find-the-set-mood-node","x":"The nodes appear after the Mood Gallery has been opened once in the session. Open the gallery, then right-click in your graph and type Mood . See Blueprint nodes .","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Moods are missing after I moved the MoodKit folder","u":"support/#fix-moods-are-missing-after-i-moved-the-moodkit-folder","x":"Keep the MoodKit folder where it is. The panel looks for moods in Content/MoodKit/Moods and MyMoods , and for your lamp styles in MyLampStyles .","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"My lights do not change with the mood","u":"support/#fix-my-lights-do-not-change-with-the-mood","x":"Static lights and baked light cannot change while a game runs. When your level has any, a row at the bottom of the Mood Gallery offers Make Lights Movable , then Build Lighting once to clear their old baked light. Save the level afterwards. See Your level's li","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"My light goes back when I edit it during a preview","u":"support/#fix-my-light-goes-back-when-i-edit-it-during-a-preview","x":"During a preview, an edited light goes back to its value from when the preview started. Change lights after Back to Original .","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Lamps in a level that streams in later do not change","u":"support/#fix-lamps-in-a-level-that-streams-in-later-do-not-change","x":"Sky, fog and colour change at once. Lamps join when you call Refresh Mood Lights after the level has loaded. See Lights added later .","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"A mood adds pools of light I did not place","u":"support/#fix-a-mood-adds-pools-of-light-i-did-not-place","x":"Some moods bring pools of light of their own, but only on levels with fewer than 3 lamps and no Mood Lamps. To never add them, untick Added lamps on the Fit tab.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Lamps do not swing in the editor","u":"support/#fix-lamps-do-not-swing-in-the-editor","x":"Nothing moves by itself in the editor. Lamps swing there only while a mood is previewed. In the game they always swing.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"The mood looks different through my game camera","u":"support/#fix-the-mood-looks-different-through-my-game-camera","x":"A camera with its own post process settings can override a mood. Leave them at their defaults where the mood should show.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"The dirt is too much for my level","u":"support/#fix-the-dirt-is-too-much-for-my-level","x":"Lower Surface wear on the Fit tab, or untick the Surface wear part. To keep one mesh clean, untick Receives Decals on it.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"I want to keep my sky from another pack","u":"support/#fix-i-want-to-keep-my-sky-from-another-pack","x":"Untick Sky on the Fit tab, and untick Sun and moon light and Sky light too if your sky brings its own. The mood keeps everything else.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"The fog has no shape","u":"support/#fix-the-fog-has-no-shape","x":"Volumetric Fog must be allowed by your scalability settings for fog to have shape. Raise them if they are set low.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"The fog bank does not show","u":"support/#fix-the-fog-bank-does-not-show","x":"The fog bank needs the mood's height fog. With Height fog unticked, the fog bank only shows if your own fog has volumetric fog on.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Wet floors hardly reflect","u":"support/#fix-wet-floors-hardly-reflect","x":"Wet floors look best with Lumen reflections, which new UE5 projects use by default. With Lumen off, wet floors reflect less.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Tree shadows move where there are no trees","u":"support/#fix-tree-shadows-move-where-there-are-no-trees","x":"With Branch shadows ticked, Moonlit Exposure, Blood Moon and Long Dusk add moving shadows of trees that are not there. Tick it only where trees would be.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Rain falls inside my building","u":"support/#fix-rain-falls-inside-my-building","x":"Mood Kit cannot know where your roofs are. Put an interior volume around each indoor space with Add Interior Volume on the Place tab. Rain, snow and fog banks stop at the first 8 rooms. See Indoor rooms .","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Lightning does not light my room","u":"support/#fix-lightning-does-not-light-my-room","x":"That is on purpose. A strike lights a room only through its doors and windows, because its light casts shadows.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"No lightning bolt shows in my own sky","u":"support/#fix-no-lightning-bolt-shows-in-my-own-sky","x":"With Sky unticked, a strike still lights your level, but no bolt or cloud flash shows in your own sky.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Snow does not settle on walls","u":"support/#fix-snow-does-not-settle-on-walls","x":"That is on purpose. Snow and ash settle only on what faces up.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"The ground changes too fast in the editor","u":"support/#fix-the-ground-changes-too-fast-in-the-editor","x":"In the editor the ground changes ten times faster than in a game, so a preview shows it.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"A Weather Zone changes the weather everywhere","u":"support/#fix-a-weather-zone-changes-the-weather-everywhere","x":"The ground is one for the whole level, so a Weather Zone changes the weather everywhere while the player is inside it. Tick Ground At Once on the zone to have the ground ready as the player arrives. See Weather Zones .","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"The mood does not show when I press Play","u":"support/#fix-the-mood-does-not-show-when-i-press-play","x":"A mood you only previewed stays out of the game. Click Apply to Level , save the level, then press Play . See Apply to Level .","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"My Mood Event does nothing in the editor","u":"support/#fix-my-mood-event-does-nothing-in-the-editor","x":"Mood Events only fire in the game, when the player walks in. Press Play and walk into the box.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"My packaged game is missing some moods","u":"support/#fix-my-packaged-game-is-missing-some-moods","x":"A packaged game only includes moods and weathers something refers to. For the in-game picker, add MoodKit/Moods to Additional Asset Directories to Cook in Project Settings. See Packaged games .","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Players need a way to turn lightning off","u":"support/#fix-players-need-a-way-to-turn-lightning-off","x":"Call Set Mood Weather Amounts with Lightning at 0, for example from your settings menu. Strikes always stay under the common limit for flashing light, but some players are still affected by it.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"The mood is gone when I open the level again","u":"support/#fix-the-mood-is-gone-when-i-open-the-level-again","x":"In the editor you see a mood only while you preview it, so the level opens as you built it. The applied mood still runs in the game, and the panel shows it with its ON tag.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"Will an update overwrite my own moods?","u":"support/#fix-will-an-update-overwrite-my-own-moods","x":"No. Your moods, lamp styles and weathers live in MyMoods , MyLampStyles and MyWeather , apart from the pack, and an update never touches them.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"I want to remove a mood from my level","u":"support/#fix-i-want-to-remove-a-mood-from-my-level","x":"Click Back to Original , then Apply to Level . Or delete the BP_MoodDirector actor.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"I want to use my own lamp meshes","u":"support/#fix-i-want-to-use-my-own-lamp-meshes","x":"Click Customize This Style and set the meshes of your copy, or untick Show Fixture on a lamp and put it inside your own mesh. See Lamp styles .","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"My level is slow with many Mood Lamps","u":"support/#fix-my-level-is-slow-with-many-mood-lamps","x":"Each Mood Lamp is a real light with shadows. Untick Cast Shadows on lamps far from the player.","k":"section"},{"p":"Support","s":"I only need some parts of a mood","u":"support/#fix-i-only-need-some-parts-of-a-mood","x":"Untick any part you do not need on the Fit tab, and your level keeps its own version of it. See Parts .","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Set Mood","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-set-mood","x":"Changes the mood of the level. Blend Seconds fades from the current look; 0 changes at once.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Clear Mood","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-clear-mood","x":"Returns the level to how it was built.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Get Mood Director","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-get-mood-director","x":"Finds the mood actor in this level, and creates one if there is none.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Set Mood Adjustments","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-set-mood-adjustments","x":"Fits the mood to this level: Brightness and Lights in stops, Fog and Surface Wear as multipliers.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Set Mood Parts","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-set-mood-parts","x":"Switches parts of the mood on or off. A part that is off leaves the level's own version of it.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Set Mood Sun Aim","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-set-mood-sun-aim","x":"Aims the sun or moon by hand. Turn is the Z rotation of the light, Height the angle above the horizon. By Hand off lets each mood choose.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Set Mood Weather","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-set-mood-weather","x":"Puts a weather on the mood: rain, snow, ash or clear skies. Leave Weather empty for the mood's own. Blend Seconds fades it in, and the ground then soaks, dries or gathers snow over time.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Set Mood Weather Amounts","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-set-mood-weather-amounts","x":"Turns the weather's rain, its falling snow and ash and its lightning, and the mood's dust and embers, up or down. 1 is as they come, 0 is none.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Set Mood Wind","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-set-mood-wind","x":"Scales the strength of the wind, where 1 is as the weather has it, and turns it. Turn is the way it blows, in degrees around the level.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Trigger Lightning","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-trigger-lightning","x":"Strikes lightning now: a flash over the level and, in the mood's sky, a bolt. It works in any weather while a mood is on. Strikes stay at least 4 seconds apart, and flash at most 3 times a second.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Trigger Blackout","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-trigger-blackout","x":"Cuts the lights for a few seconds, then brings them back. It needs a mood to be active.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Set Mood Lamp Group","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-set-mood-lamp-group","x":"Switches every Mood Lamp whose Group is this on or off. Leave Group empty for every Mood Lamp.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Flicker Mood Lamps","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-flicker-mood-lamps","x":"Makes every Mood Lamp whose Group is this flicker for a few seconds. Leave Group empty for every Mood Lamp.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Swing Mood Lamps","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-swing-mood-lamps","x":"Knocks every hanging Mood Lamp whose Group is this, so it swings and slowly settles. Leave Group empty for every Mood Lamp.","k":"section"},{"p":"Blueprint nodes","s":"Refresh Mood Lights","u":"blueprint-nodes/#node-refresh-mood-lights","x":"Call this after streaming in a level, so its lamps join the current mood.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Sealed Dark","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"No light but what you carry. Heavy, wet air. Very dark. A soft beam comes from the player's view and lights stained floors and walls, with dust hanging in it.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Failing Power","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Weak, sick lamps stutter and die one by one. Weak yellow-green lamps in haze, with rust and damp on the walls. Some lamps are dead, and now and then one stutters and comes back.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Blind Fog","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Pale fog swallows the world, and ash drifts down in it. Fog hides everything past a few metres and windows turn blank white. Lamps glow in the fog, and pale ash drifts down outside.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Moonlit Exposure","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"A cold moon, wet ground and shadows of unseen branches. A cold moon over wet ground, fog rolling along the floor and slow cloud shadows. Indoors it is dark, with moonlight through the windows.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Bright Wrong","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Bleached daylight under a black sun. Too bright, too quiet. Washed-out grey daylight under a black sun. Dusty, cracked surfaces, blank white windows and air that shimmers a little.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Red Alert","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Emergency beacons sweep red light through thick air. Deep red. The lamps pulse slowly brighter and darker, about once every 2 seconds, through hazy air.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Last Candle","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"One small flame, and a dark that goes on forever. Warm, wavering light around the player that falls off quickly into dark. Small embers rise.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Toxic Haze","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Sick yellow-green gas rolls along the ground. Sick yellow-green light and gas that rolls low along the ground. Now and then a lamp flickers.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Blood Moon","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"A huge red moon, and everything under it looks wrong. A huge red moon, red light on a dark floor and red windows. Everything under it looks wrong.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Ash Fall","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"A burnt sun through smoke. Ash falls, embers rise. A burnt orange sun through smoke. Ash falls and greys the ground, embers rise and surfaces look sooty.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Drowned","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Cold rain hammers standing water. Everything is soaked. Cold and blue-green. Rain hammers down, floors are soaked and reflective, and puddles grow.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Found Footage","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"An old camcorder, its weak light and damaged tape. Almost no colour, and old tape: lines, noise, a bar rolling up the picture and a noisy strip at the bottom.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Liminal Hum","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Flat yellow light, stained floors, and nobody here. Flat, yellow light that is too even, with stained walls and floors, and nobody here.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Long Dusk","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"The sun is gone but the last light stays, cold and orange. The sun is gone but a warm glow stays in the sky. Deep shadow, and pools of orange lamplight.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Blinds Drawn","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Hard light cuts through half-shut blinds. Smoke hangs in the bars. Hard light through half-shut blinds: bars of light and shade across floors and walls, smoke in the bars, and nearly no colour.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Sodium Night","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Orange street lamps buzz over wet, empty ground. The shadows go blue. Orange street lamps over wet ground. Everything they touch turns orange, and the shadows between them go blue.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Neon Static","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Pink and cyan signs bleed into the dark. Something is wrong with the signal. Lamps turn pink and cyan, like signs bleeding into the dark. Wet floors catch both colours, and the picture breaks up a little.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Interrogation","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"One hard lamp overhead. Outside its circle, nothing. One hard white lamp overhead and black everywhere outside its circle, with dust turning in the cone.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"From Below","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Low red lights on the floor throw every shadow up the walls. Low red lights on the floor shine up, so every shadow climbs the walls, and low fog glows red.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Camera Flash","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Pitch dark. Every few seconds a flash shows what is there. Pitch dark. Every 4 seconds a camera flash lights the view for a moment, hard and white, then the dark comes back.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Backlit","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"A white sun behind the fog turns everything into black shapes. A low white sun behind thick fog. Everything between you and it turns into black shapes against the glow.","k":"section"},{"p":"The moods","s":"Night Shift","u":"moods/#every-mood","x":"Only the lamps are on. Warm pools of light, and black between them. Only the lamps are on: warm pools of light, and black between them.","k":"section"}];
